<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss short money easy on quiet Friday.</title>
<headline>Swiss short money easy on quiet Friday.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss short-term money was easy as business stalled between the Christmas and New Year's holidays.</p>
<p>Tomorrow/next was quoted at 1.50/75 and traders said it was expected to reamin around 1.50.</p>
<p>One-week rates, which had ratched up to over 4.75 at the start of the week on bank demands, were back down to 3.50/4.00.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
